.TH "CHECK_INTERFACES" "1" "April 2026" "NMS_Tools" "SNMP Interface State Checker"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
\f[B]check_interfaces\f[R] \[em] SNMP-based network interface state and
health checker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]check_interfaces\f[R] -H -C options
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]check_interfaces\f[R] queries network devices via SNMP to evaluate
interface operational state, admin state, speed, duplex, and error
counters.
.PP
It is suitable for: - Monitoring switches and routers
.PD 0
.P
.PD
- Detecting interface failures
.PD 0
.P
.PD
- Automation pipelines
.PD 0
.P
.PD
- Deterministic SNMP diagnostics
.SH OPTIONS
.SS SNMP
.PP
\f[B]-H, \[en]host \f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Target device.
.PP
\f[B]-C, \[en]community \f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
SNMP community string.
.PP
\f[B]\[en]version <1|2c>\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
SNMP version.
.SS Filtering
.PP
\f[B]\[en]match \f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Include interfaces matching pattern.
.PP
\f[B]\[en]exclude \f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Exclude interfaces matching pattern.
.SS Debugging
.PP
\f[B]\[en]debug-snmp\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Show SNMP request/response details.
.PP
\f[B]\[en]verbose\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Show per-interface metrics.
.SS Output Modes
.PP
\f[B]\[en]json\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Emit structured JSON.
.PP
\f[B]\[en]quiet\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Suppress human-readable output.
.SH EXIT CODES
.PP
\f[B]0\f[R] \[em] All required interfaces OK
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]1\f[R] \[em] Non-critical issue
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]2\f[R] \[em] Critical interface failure
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]3\f[R] \[em] Unknown error
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Check all interfaces:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
check_interfaces -H switch01 -C public
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Filter by name:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
check_interfaces -H switch01 -C public --match \[dq]uplink\[dq]
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Debug SNMP:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
check_interfaces -H switch01 -C public --debug-snmp
\f[R]
.fi
